.TH murk-setup-merge-driver 1  "setup-merge-driver " 
.SH NAME
murk\-setup\-merge\-driver \- Configure git to use murk\*(Aqs merge driver for vault files named `*.murk` or `.murk.*` (experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk setup\-merge\-driver\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure git to use murk\*(Aqs merge driver for vault files named `*.murk` or `.murk.*` (experimental)
.PP
Adds `*.murk merge=murk` and `.murk.* merge=murk` to the `.gitattributes` at the root of the working tree, and sets `merge.murk.*` in git config. Changes nothing when git config already sets a `merge.murk.driver` that murk did not write, or when the git attributes already give vault files another `merge` attribute.
.PP
The driver merges three sides that murk reads as vaults. It merges a file that cannot be a vault as text. When a side is or could be a vault but murk cannot read every side, the driver exits 1 and writes both sides into the file between conflict markers. Valid JSON could be a vault only when it has a top\-level `recipients`, `secrets`, `meta`, `vault_name` or `vault_id` key. Other text could be a vault when it starts with `{` or uses one of these names as a JSON key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
